From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: vfe-17x: Add the focus statistics

BFStats23 as the Windows driver programs it: two IIR filters with coring
and a gamma map on the green pixels, up to 178 regions from a ROI table
of 180 entries (with an empty one before and after them), records
written by bus write master 14 after an 8-byte header into the
statistics buffer, after the AWB grid. A statistics buffer completes
when every write master the frame was set up with is done; addresses are
queued only for the write masters that write the next frame.

With two IFEs each sees one stripe of the frame and the regions are in
frame coordinates. Let the parameters say how the regions split between
the stripes: the first num_left regions are measured by the left stripe
(the master), the others by the right stripe (the slave), in the columns
of its own input. Each part follows the order rules of a single IFE on
its own, and the record of each region keeps its index in the whole
list. The focus write master writes its header before its records, so
the right stripe's records get a fixed slot, bf[IFE17X_BF_DUAL_RIGHT],
with its header at the end of the slot before.

The statistics address of frame k + 1 was queued when the AWB grid of
frame k was done, at its end. In the 60 fps binned mode of the ov13b10
the next frame starts about 0.4 ms later; when the interrupt came later
than that, the write masters found no address and skipped the frame, and
every statistics buffer from then on held the frame after its request's.
Queue the statistics addresses when the frame is settled: at epoch 0
with the image buffer and the parameters, at a late join, or at a new
epoch 1 three quarters into the frame, which ends the join window and
sends a frame no buffer joined to the scratch buffer. An epoch 1 missed,
or seen with the next SOF, queues no late address: the write masters
skip that frame.

Also:
- Take the output lock before the meta lock in the buffer queue path;
  the interrupt takes both, and the meta lock with interrupts on locked
  up on any QBUF.
- Stopping the statistics node while the pixel path runs returns the
  queued buffers, waits until the hardware is done with the settled and
  held ones (three frame periods and 100 ms, from 0.5 to 5 s at most),
  then fails the rest. A pixel path stop without a reset (another line
  keeps the VFE) stops the statistics and their write masters.
- Handle the bus done bits whenever the bus status has them, not only
  with bit 9 of status 0, read before them.
- A failed stream start stops the subdevs it started; a node whose line
  already streams for another node cannot start (-EBUSY); a wedged VFE
  errors only the queues that stream.
- The rail level is taken from the rates the clocks have when any vote
  changes, so a shared camnoc_axi raised by another VFE keeps its level.
- A disabled white balance block sets unity gains; one AWB grid column
  counts as two with dual IFE; every block's reserved fields and value
  ranges are checked when queued.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
